WEBVTT

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:10.032
A resource is something a program gets, uses, and

00:00:10.032 --> 00:00:10.656
releases.

00:00:10.656 --> 00:00:13.916
Its lifetime is the time between getting it and

00:00:13.916 --> 00:00:14.817
releasing it.

00:00:14.817 --> 00:00:18.077
NamedResource models that lifetime with printed

00:00:18.077 --> 00:00:18.701
messages.

00:00:18.701 --> 00:00:21.059
These objects only print messages.

00:00:38.779 --> 00:00:42.100
AutoCloseable is an interface that requires a close

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:42.556
method.

00:00:42.556 --> 00:00:46.072
Try-with-resources declares objects inside parentheses

00:00:46.072 --> 00:00:46.723
after try.

00:00:46.723 --> 00:00:49.848
Java calls close on the successfully initialized

00:00:49.848 --> 00:00:53.104
resources when control leaves the block, including

00:00:53.104 --> 00:00:54.927
when an exception leaves it.

00:00:54.927 --> 00:00:58.053
The last object initialized is the first closed.

00:00:58.053 --> 00:01:00.201
This is reverse resource closure.

00:01:00.201 --> 00:01:03.327
If the running Java program is forcibly stopped,

00:01:03.327 --> 00:01:04.629
cleanup may not run.

00:01:04.928 --> 00:01:08.349
Predict the complete output, including the order of

00:01:08.349 --> 00:01:11.904
construction, work, closing, and the final statement.

00:01:11.904 --> 00:01:15.459
Use the order of declarations and the reverse closing

00:01:15.459 --> 00:01:15.794
rule.

00:01:15.794 --> 00:01:17.203
Pause before running.

00:01:22.581 --> 00:01:25.426
The constructors print first, then second.

00:01:25.426 --> 00:01:26.848
The body prints Work.

00:01:26.848 --> 00:01:29.354
Java then closes second before first.

00:01:29.354 --> 00:01:32.266
Done appears after both close calls finish.

00:01:32.266 --> 00:01:35.856
The try statement supplies those calls automatically.

00:01:35.856 --> 00:01:39.107
Our printed messages show exactly when each step

00:01:39.107 --> 00:01:39.581
occurs.

00:01:39.664 --> 00:01:43.160
Swap the two resource declarations, keeping each name

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:44.215
with its object.

00:01:44.215 --> 00:01:47.777
Predict the new output and explain which rule controls

00:01:47.777 --> 00:01:48.964
the closing order.
